Challenge 2 -- shopping_buyer.py manual runs

Setup: python spawn_shops.py --count 20 --out directory.json
  -> 20 real Agent Cards collected (ports 9800-9819), item subsets and price
     multipliers varied per shop (see spawn_shops.py's ITEM_SETS / mult formula),
     e.g.:
       Shop 01 (lamp)               -> Sells: lamp.
       Shop 02 (chair)              -> Sells: chair.
       Shop 03 (bookshelf)          -> Sells: bookshelf.
       Shop 04 (lamp/chair)         -> Sells: lamp, chair.
       ... (20 total, see directory.json)

=== Bug found and fixed before these runs ===
First attempt: ask_harness_candidates("lamp", shops) returned
  'CANDIDATES Shop 01, Shop 08, Shop 15, Shop 04, Shop 11, ...'
-- the harness dropped the trailing "(item, item)" from the full shop name
when repeating it back, so exact-string validation against the directory
rejected every single name -> candidates for lamp: []. Fixed by resolving a
returned name to the one directory name it is a PREFIX of, instead of
requiring an exact match (see ask_harness_candidates in shopping_buyer.py).

=== Run 1: shopping list [lamp, chair, bookshelf], budget 500 (too tight) ===
$ python shopping_buyer.py --directory directory.json --list shopping_list.json --budget 500
  candidates for lamp: ['Shop 01 (lamp)', 'Shop 08 (lamp)', 'Shop 15 (lamp)']
  bought lamp from Shop 15 (lamp) at 103.0 (remaining budget: 397.0)
  candidates for chair: ['Shop 02 (chair)', 'Shop 09 (chair)', 'Shop 16 (chair)']
  bought chair from Shop 02 (chair) at 220.0 (remaining budget: 177.0)
  candidates for bookshelf: ['Shop 03 (bookshelf)', 'Shop 10 (bookshelf)', 'Shop 17 (bookshelf)']
  could not buy bookshelf within remaining budget 177.0
  -> all_items_bought: false (budget too tight for this list, not a bug -- the
     buyer correctly refused to overspend rather than exceed the budget)

