=== Run 3: duplicate-item guard, list [lamp, chair, bookshelf, lamp], budget 650 ===
$ python shopping_buyer.py --directory directory.json --list shopping_list_dup_test.json --budget 650
  bought lamp from Shop 08 (lamp) at 120.0 (remaining budget: 530.0)
  bought chair from Shop 02 (chair) at 220.0 (remaining budget: 310.0)
  bought bookshelf from Shop 03 (bookshelf) at 250.0 (remaining budget: 60.0)
  skip lamp: already bought          <-- the second "lamp" entry was skipped in code,
                                           never sent to any shop a second time
  -> {"all_items_bought": true, "within_budget": true, "no_duplicates": true}

=== Known limitation (documented honestly, not fixed) ===
shop_for_item() negotiates with up to 3 candidate shops AT ONCE (asyncio.gather)
and keeps only the cheapest one that actually closed. If more than one
candidate's negotiation reaches TASK_STATE_COMPLETED in the same batch, the
"losing" shop(s) also believe they made a real sale (there is no A2A operation
to undo a COMPLETED task) -- the buyer just never records or pays for it. This
is a real tradeoff of negotiating with several shops at once rather than one
at a time, and is left as-is rather than engineered around, within this
assignment's time budget.
